            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This will break the `:bcd` behavior for that buffer permanently, right? What if the user switches back and wants to run `:!`?\n\nAlso, I think its actually fine if `1-` is useless; it will still do something if the user has an autocommand which changes the buffer-local directory (e.g. to the project root), and changing the behavior of `1-` in directory buffers could actually mess that up.",
            "commit_id": "ac888660ee1de8a9e2cfeb65475bcbc61e57db5c",
            "created_at": "2026-08-10T00:36:33Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@ end, { silent = true, desc = 'Open directory entry' })\n \n vim.keymap.set('n', '<Plug>(nvim-dir-up)', function()\n   if vim.v.count == 1 then\n+    if vim.b.nvim_dir ~= nil then\n+      vim.cmd('bcd!')\n+    end",
